## BMStrings — After Six's copy. Same key names as the day game (main.gd is a fork and
## reads the same keys), re-meant for the night: a node is a person and what they want;
## the inbox is her desk; the review is the confrontation; the standup is the security
## round. en + zh-Hans ship together (PLAN.md locale rule). Never hardcode a user-visible
## string in a scene.
##
## The fiction keeps the DLsite golden tags where they fit (ops/adult_forks/beat_monday_map.md
## §2): the scene is part of the node system (戦闘エロ), the night rule rewrites what is
## normal (常識改変), colleagues with history (同居/幼なじみ), her offer (色仕掛け), the
## building after hours (退廃/背徳), the state she comes back in (トランス/暗示). Everyone is
## an adult and everything is consensual in the fiction — she comes back on her own.
class_name BMStrings


## The CJK face each language is drawn with. It lives here, beside the tables themselves,
## because it is a property OF the table: a language's strings and the font that can draw
## them are one fact, and splitting them is how the game ended up offering Japanese against
## a font with no kana in it. main.gd installs these as fallbacks and the test suite checks
## each table against its own file.
##
## One subset per script family, never one shared face -- see main.gd's note.
const CJK_FONT := {
	"zh": "res://assets/fonts/NotoSansCJKsc-subset.ttf",
	"ja": "res://assets/fonts/NotoSansCJKjp-subset.ttf",
}
const CJK_FONT_DEFAULT := "res://assets/fonts/NotoSansCJKsc-subset.ttf"


static func font_for(code: String) -> String:
	return str(CJK_FONT.get(code, CJK_FONT_DEFAULT))

