##
## STANDARD.md item 7: ja is the priority, because 507 of the 581 DLsite works in
## ops/market/dlsite_data/ are Japanese and this title is the DLsite bet. It is also the
## rule that says never offer a language you did not actually translate -- Floor 13 shipped
## ja/ko/es whose story files held Chinese prose and someone had to switch them off.
##
## So every one of the 245 keys in EN is written here, in Japanese, and the build test
## proves the count matches rather than trusting this comment. Two things that are NOT
## translation and were checked separately:
##
##   * The bundled CJK face was a 342-glyph subset cut for the Chinese strings and it
##     contains NO kana at all -- not one. Shipping this table against that font would
##     have rendered the whole language as tofu boxes while every string check on disk
##     passed, which is the studio memory `verification-that-lies` exactly. The ja text is
##     subset from Noto Sans CJK **JP**, not SC: a JP reader sees Chinese glyph forms for
##     the shared kanji immediately, and no check on disk would catch that either.
##   * `{n}`-style placeholders are kept verbatim; t() replaces them by literal match, so a
##     translated brace is a string that silently prints "{n}".
